    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nNestled away in the leafy and much desired development of Hampton Green this lovely three bed end-of-terrace family home offers many exciting features and a great location. The property offers a good sized walled back garden with a lawn, and a raised patio area for outdoor dining. Excellent transport links provide easy access to town by bus and car . The Phoenix Park,the M50 north and south bound are accessible within 5 mins of the location.\n\nDNG are delighted to present to the market number 6 Hampton Green a fabulous family home. Excellent features include  solar panels (1.9kW Solar PV system) ,2 electric showers.The bathrooms have been recently refurbished to a high level. There are also newly fitted wardrobes in bedrooms 1 and two. Off-street parking is available.\n\n\nAccommodation briefly consists of; entrance hall, living room, dining room,kitchen, downstairs W/C, 3 bedrooms one of which is en-suite, family bathroom The property features a generous back garden with concrete shed ,there is also off-street parking to the front.\n\nThe property is within walking distance of The Phoenix Park, local shops and selection of excellent schools. Dublin City Centre and the M50 are within easy reach and the area is also well serviced by excellent public transport links to Dublin City Centre from the Navan Road.\n\nViewing by appointment with DNG estate agents in Phibsboro 01 8300989 contact local agent: Michelle Keeley MIPAV MMCEP, Brian McGee MIPAV, Isabel O'Neill MIPAV, Vincent Mullen MIPAV & Ciaran Jones MIPAV,Isabel O`Neill and Leah Barry."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - 1.29m x 5.24m\nEntrance hall with laminate flooring, there is access to understairs storage.\n\nGuest Water - \nWater closet with tiled floor , thee is a W/C and a W.H.B.\n\nLiving Room - 5.16m x 3.38m\nLiving room with focal point fireplace with marble hearth, there is a decorative wooden mantle piece.\n\nDining room - 3.8m x 2.5m\nDining room is spacious on bright and faces the back garden.There is laminate flooring.\n\nKitchen - 2.7m x 5.07m\nKitchen tiled floor faces back garden,there are floor and wall presses. There is spot lighting.\n\nLanding - 2.19m x 2.92\nLanding area with access to attic, which can be converted subject to planning. There is a hotpress off the landing with shelving for storage.\n\nBathroom - 1.95m x 2.3m\nFamily bathroom with W/C and bath.There is a window for light and ventilation.There is a chrome heated towel rail.There are porcelain tiles.\n\nBedroom 1 - 2.9m x 4.55m\nSpacious diuble bedroom en-suite, located at the front of the house.There is built-in wardrobes for excellent storage.En-suite with walk-in shower with built-in recess. There is a W.H.B with electronic mirror offer it.There is a W/C.\n\nBedroom 2 - 3.10m x 3.31m\nDouble bedroom located at the back of the house with with sliderobes for good storage.\n\nBedroom 3 - 2.89m x 2m\nBedroom with laminate flooring located at the front of the house .There is a built-in wardrobes.\n\nOutside - \nTo the front there is off street parking and a side garden with access to a secure side entrance.There is a large walled back garden with with conrete shed and pedestrian path to raised patio area.\n\n"
      },
